{{notice|This page is for Easter eggs only. Easter eggs include inside jokes, pop culture references, and any similar reference to something ''outside the Elder Scrolls games''. For other points of interest, like [[Skyrim:Unfinished Quests|unfinished quests]], or [[Skyrim:Elder Scrolls Historical References|references to other games in the ''Elder Scrolls'' series]], please see the appropriate pages.}}

'''Easter eggs''' are secrets that the developers put in the game to give people a laugh when they find them. [[Skyrim:Skyrim|Skyrim]] has a large number of such jokes. Easter eggs differ from in-game references in that they have been intentionally hidden from the player and are unusual with regards to their surroundings.

'''Cultural references''' are objects, characters, or events in the game that refer to a specific element of popular culture; they differ from Easter eggs in that they are usually integrated into the game world, and strong parallels can be drawn between the in-game event and the specific work being referenced. Cultural references also include allusions to elements of real-world culture, such as historical events and folklore.

If you think you have found an Easter egg or reference, please post your idea on this article's [[Skyrim talk:Easter Eggs|talk page]] before adding it to this article.

==Easter Eggs==
===Aiming for the Bucket===
* A room in the main area of [[Skyrim:Fort Dunstad|Fort Dunstad]] appears to be a latrine. In this room, on a stone shelf beside one of the "toilets" is a [[Skyrim:Potion of True Shot|Potion of True Shot]], a possible joke by the game's developers about aiming during urination.

===Erik the Slayer===
* The character [[Skyrim:Erik|Erik]] is based on [[General:Erik West|Erik West]], who was known as "ImmoktheSlayer" online and who died of cancer in May 2011. The Make-a-Wish Foundation arranged for Erik to visit Bethesda Softwork's offices during the development of the game, leading to the subsequent creation of the character as a tribute.{{ref|RoyStaff, Matthew K. [https://www.salemnews.com/news/local_news/stricken-by-cancer-teen-never-stopped-smiling/article_1b934673-edf9-5272-906e-c097a0225c63.html Stricken by cancer, teen never stopped smiling — Salem News] (2011-05-23). [https://web.archive.org/web/20160414195047/https://www.salemnews.com/news/local_news/stricken-by-cancer-teen-never-stopped-smiling/article_1b934673-edf9-5272-906e-c097a0225c63.html Archived] from the original on 2016-04-14.}}

===The Lusty Riekling{{DB}}===
* In [[Skyrim:Benkongerike|Benkongerike]] there is a riekling hut tucked away all by itself. It is full of dozens of copies of ''[[Skyrim:The Lusty Argonian Maid|The Lusty Argonian Maid]]'' and multiple bundles of linen cloth. ''The Lusty Argonian Maid'', a pornographic play, and the linen cloths, which are similar to tissues or any other device used to clean up a mess, are both closely associated with masturbation. There is also a telekinesis spell tome hidden under the books, and in Skyrim, telekinesis is used to make items come to you...

===Moving Statues===
* When entering [[Skyrim:Sovngarde (place)|Sovngarde]] during the main quest, several of the statues lining the stone steps that lead down from the portal to [[Skyrim:Skuldafn|Skuldafn]] will rotate as you descend.

